This repository is licensed under two different licences. Which one applies
depends on which directory a file is in, and the split is deliberate.

    engine/     GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only
                Full text in engine/LICENSE

    shell/      MIT
    agent/      MIT
                Full text in shell/LICENSE and agent/LICENSE

    everything  MIT, on the same terms as the shell
    else

No single-licence label describes this repository, so please do not read
one from a badge. The engine is the part that carries the AGPL obligation:
if you run a modified version of it as a network service, you must offer
the source of your modified version to that service's users. Running it
privately carries no such obligation, and the MIT parts carry none at all.

The two components are joined by exactly one adapter module,
shell/src/optiondesk/engine_bridge.py, so the boundary can be checked with
a single grep. The shell runs without the engine installed and reports
Greeks as unavailable rather than computing them.

A commercial licence removing the AGPL obligations is available from the
copyright holder.

See LICENSES.md for the reasoning, THIRD-PARTY.md for what is vendored and
under what terms, and DISCLAIMER.md for what this software is and is not.

